<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Colima sees 10 pct rise in iron output.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Colima sees 10 pct rise in iron output.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's western state of Guadalajara will boost iron production by 10 percent in 1996 from 2.72 million tonnes in 1995, a mining official said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Sergio Andrade, Colima head of the Mineral Resources Council, said the output has been raised since a mine in Cerro Nahuatl in the west of the state begun producing at the end of last year. The mine is owned by Las Encinas S.A., a unit of Hylsa.</p>
<p>--Veronica Galan, Guadalajara newsroom, +523 817-0440</p>
